      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Getting Started with CloudScale Stream API\n\nWelcome to CloudScale Stream API! This guide will help you get started from obtaining your API key to making your first authenticated GET request.\n\n## Step 1: Obtain Your API Key\n\nTo use CloudScale Stream API, you need to obtain an API key. Sign up for an account on our website and navigate to the API keys section. Generate a new API key and securely store it for future use.\n\n## Step 2: Set Up Your Development Environment\n\nInstall the required libraries and dependencies for your preferred programming language. CloudScale Stream API supports multiple languages, including Python, Java, and Node.js.\n\n## Step 3: Make Your First Authenticated GET Request\n\nTo make an authenticated GET request, follow these steps:\n\n1. Import the necessary libraries in your code.\n2. Set up your API key and endpoint URL.\n3. Use the `requests.get()` method to send a GET request to the desired endpoint.\n4. Handle the response and display the result.\n\nCongratulations! You have successfully made your first authenticated GET request to CloudScale Stream API.",
